<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Herbs</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Druid (guild level 1), Ranger (guild level 12, up to 75%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>herbs              (heal yourself)
herbs &lt;someone&gt;    (heal someone with you)
</pre>
<p>You search the land around you for healing herbs, and use them at once to 
treat yourself or someone else in the room. It costs 20 endurance, and you 
must be standing. The better your search goes, the more hit points it 
heals.
</p><p>Fields and forests are full of herbs, and easy to search. Hills, swamps 
and water are harder, mountains harder still, and the desert hardest. In 
cities, indoors, and on snow or ice, nothing grows that heals. Fail, and 
you find nothing, or something you'd better not risk using.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
